{"duration_api_ms":155780,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"02ed7ec7-7757-4cd4-a26a-7af76754dab3","total_cost_usd":0.22104400000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16320,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15576,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10608},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16320,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15576,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16320},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15576,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16320,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.22104400000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10608,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is a one-dimensional sweep in flight_path_angle at the corner D≈3.385, bluntness 1.2, cone 70. It runs from about (227k W/m², 417.9 K) at gamma -1.5 to about (274.6k, 391.1 K) at gamma -3.57. Three limits pin this corner. Heatshield mass fraction caps D at about 3.38524. Peak g depends almost only on gamma and reaches 12.0 at -3.57. Cone 70 is the variable maximum, and bluntness above about 1.2 at cone 70 fails the cd_fore surrogate's convex-hull check. The last four rounds moved normalised hypervolume by less than 0.003 in total, so it is saturated.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-25994855d0b4: D=3.3852, gamma=-3.57 gives g margin 4e-5 and mass margin 2.7e-5, so gamma and D are both at their limits.\",\"C-948029610632 (gamma -1.5) and C-25994855d0b4 (gamma -3.57) are the two ends of a smooth convex front.\",\"Mass margin vs D at bluntness 1.2, cone 70: C-053e6577c074 (3.38) 0.0031, C-9311986cd363 (3.383) 0.0013, C-294c231fb7c2 (3.3852) 2.7e-5. This is about -0.59 per metre, so the margin reaches zero near D=3.38524. Margin is the same across gamma.\",\"Seven geometry failures (C-4aa35af3d6a3, C-39bfab3c832b, C-35e288c12205, C-660a8eef4199 and others) all have bluntness of 1.205 or more at cone 70. C-460ff98d4dde (bluntness 1.2, cone 69) also fails. Bluntness and cone are therefore capped at the hull corner (1.2, 70).\",\"C-d883f15f56c5 (D 3.37, bluntness 1.05) and C-3583b7488cf2 (D 3.3) are dominated by the sweep, so lowering D or bluntness does not help.\",\"Slopes along the front are convex: dT/dF is -0.68 K per 1k W/m² between gamma -1.5 and -2.5, and -0.47 between -2.5 and -3.57. Linear chords across gaps therefore underestimate the dominated area.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux scales roughly as sqrt(rho_peak/Rn), and bondline temperature follows the heat load, which is roughly flux times pulse time. Both improve with larger D. The mass-fraction limit stops D near 3.3852. Steeper gamma shortens the pulse, so temperature falls and flux rises, until the g cap at gamma≈-3.57. The remaining hypervolume gain therefore comes from filling the gaps on the convex front and from a slightly larger D (3.38524) that lowers flux by about 5 W/m². This flux effect relies on prior scaling knowledge, consistent with the tables. Where the front is already sampled densely, gains are near 1e-5. I spend the round on gap-filling with interpolated predictions and no risky off-corner exploration.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Expected gains are tiny. Mass margin at D=3.38524 is about +3e-6 by linear extrapolation, so a small nonlinearity could make those points infeasible. Interpolated flux and temperature should be within about 0.3% and 0.3 K. I cannot exclude a better region outside the hull corner, but geometry failures make it unreachable with these variables.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Anchor at the shallow end with the marginally larger D allowed by mass fraction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38524,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227210,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.87,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether D=3.38524 stays inside the mass-fraction limit and gives a small flux gain at the shallow end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the 0.2 deg gap between gamma -1.7 and -1.9 at maximum D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38524,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233280,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the largest gap on the convex front; the chord underestimates the dominated area.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.7 and -1.9.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.85},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":234340,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.26,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap on the front at the known-safe D=3.3852.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.9 and -2.05.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.95},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236490,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.74,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D on the front at gamma -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38524,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242060,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.09,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves on C-2d7e6dba2267, which was run at D=3.385.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.28 and -2.42.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":245490,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.04,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly larger D at gamma -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38524,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":248990,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.04,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves on C-df9f7a25badc, which was run at D=3.385.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.5 and -2.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":250170,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.41,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a gap on the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-25994855d0b4\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.7 and -2.78.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":254900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.92,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_sim